 "scenes": [
  {
   "turn": 1,
   "narration": "The salt air of Tortuga carries the stench of spilled rum, roasting meat, and rotting fish. You stand on the sun-baked timber of the docks, the deed to a weathered sloop clutched tightly in your hand. She is a beautiful thing in her own rugged way, her mast cutting clean against the bright Caribbean sky. You won her fair and square on a final roll of the dice, and now she is yours to command. \n\n\"A fine piece of wood, if she doesn't take on water at the first swell,\" a gravelly voice rumbles beside you. \n\nYou turn to find Captain Edward \"Blackbeak\" Teach leaning against a stack of cargo crates. Smoke from the slow-matches tucked beneath his tricorn hat drifts lazily around his bearded face. His dark eyes size you up with cold, calculated interest, weighing whether you are a captain worth knowing or just another fool destined for the gallows. He nods toward your new vessel. \"A sloop like that needs a crew, and a crew needs gold. What is your play, Captain?\"",
   "player_action": null
  }
 ],
 "choices": [
  "Address Blackbeak and ask him for advice on recruiting a crew.",
  "Inspect the sloop's hull and sails to ensure she is seaworthy.",
  "Head to the nearest tavern to celebrate your win and buy drinks."
